  "notes": "A ずる verb (classical サ{変|へん} variant). The modern form {案|あん}じる (ichidan) is also widely used. Both {案|あん}ずる and {案|あん}じる are correct. The ずる form sounds slightly more literary.\n\nPROVERB:\n{案|あん}ずるより{産|う}むが{易|やす}し — literally \"giving birth is easier than worrying about it.\" Meaning: things are often easier than anticipated; don't overthink it.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {身|み}を{案|あん}じる: to worry about someone's safety\n- {将来|しょうらい}を{案|あん}じる: to worry about the future\n- {安否|あんぴ}を{案|あん}じる: to worry about someone's safety",
